course: dictionary
lesson: 14822
title: Quicker
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Quicker is the comparing form of quick. We use it when we put two things side by side and ask which one takes less time or moves at a higher speed. «The bus is quicker than the train.» The bus takes less time, so it is the faster choice.
explain: Quick, quicker and quickest work like steps on a ladder. Quick describes one thing, quicker compares two things, and quickest picks out the top one of three or more. «Sam is quick, Ava is quicker, and Ben is the quickest of all.» When you are comparing two things, choose quicker.
explain: Quicker can also mean cleverer at understanding or reacting fast. «Priya is quicker at mental maths than her friends.» Here it is not about running or moving, but about how fast her mind works. To check your meaning, swap in faster: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Quicker is the comparative form of quick, used to compare two things.
fact: «Quicker» means faster: taking less time, or moving at a higher speed than something else.
fact: «Quicker» can also mean good at understanding or reacting fast, as in «quicker at mental maths».
fact: The other forms are quick (one thing) and quickest (the top one of three or more).
fact: Useful phrases include «quicker than», «much quicker», «the quicker the better» and «a quicker way».
exercise: «The train is quicker than the bus.» What does quicker mean here? | Is more crowded | Is painted blue | Takes more time | *Takes less time
exercise: Which word compares two things: quick, quicker or quickest? | quickest | *quicker | quick
exercise: «Priya is quicker at mental maths than her friends.» What does quicker mean here? | Taller | *Faster at thinking | Quieter | Slower at running
test: «Ben is the quickest runner in the team, and Ella is quicker than Sam.» Who is faster, Ella or Sam? | Nobody | Sam | *Ella | Ben
test: The walk through the park is ___ than the walk round the lake. Which word fits? | quick | quickest | *quicker | quickly
exam: «Max finished his homework much quicker than usual.» What does quicker mean here? | Wrote in pencil | Wrote in a louder voice | *Took less time | Took more care
